# Agentic / implementation routing

**ADF status mirror: COMPLETE ADF-A–ADF-H; ADF-EX-17 DEFERRED VERIFICATION; FOUNDATION EXIT ACCEPTED.**

**CKR status mirror: COMPLETE CKR-A–CKR-K; CKR EXIT ACCEPTED.**

**DPTN status mirror: COMPLETE DPTN-A–DPTN-B; NEXT DPTN-C; IMPLEMENTATION 001-A BLOCKED ON DPTN EXIT.**

ADF and CKR are complete/accepted. DPTN-A–B are complete/accepted. DPTN-C is NEXT / READY / NOT STARTED. Implementation 001-A is BLOCKED / NOT STARTED until DPTN-G exit acceptance and a later explicit human-selected implementation task.

Primary shared authority remains root `AGENTS.md`, `docs/agentic_development_foundation/authority_scope_policy.md`, the CKR ownership inventory, accepted ADF scope/security mechanics and live DPTN topology authority.

For a known stable ID, use `python3 scripts/agentic/resolve_stable_id.py <ID>` for the **current** canonical locator. Use `--history` only for provenance/history. For unknown semantic location, use one bounded `knowledge/index.md` route, then the current canonical owner.

`docs/history/` is provenance-only. The cleared `docs/concepts/`, `docs/reference/` and `docs/decisions/` names are vacant/unassigned. DPTN-C canonical promotion requires explicit human selection and an accepted atomic cutover; it is not authorized by DPTN-B closure.

Do not infer authority from history, path vacancy, move maps, OKF, resolver output alone, recency, search order, Git history, vendor skill, tool memory, source availability or path presence.
